---
export const prerender = true;

import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Container from '../components/Container.astro';
import Eyebrow from '../components/Eyebrow.astro';

const lastUpdated = 'September 1, 2026';
---

<Layout title="Terms of Service — ScreenshotTextEditor" description="Acceptable use, content credentials, and rate limits for ScreenshotTextEditor.">
	<Nav />

	<main>
		<section class="border-b border-hairline py-16">
			<Container class="max-w-2xl">
				<Eyebrow>Legal</Eyebrow>
				<h1 class="mt-3 text-[32px] font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink">Terms of service</h1>
				<p class="mt-2 text-[13px] text-mute">Last updated {lastUpdated}</p>
			</Container>
		</section>

		<section class="py-16">
			<Container class="max-w-2xl prose-content text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-body">
				<p>
					ScreenshotTextEditor edits text inside images convincingly enough that the result is meant to be
					indistinguishable from an original screenshot. That capability is the product — and it's also exactly what
					makes it attractive to people trying to fake something. These terms exist mainly to draw that line clearly.
				</p>

				<h2>Acceptable use</h2>
				<p>You may not use this service to create or edit an image that:</p>
				<ul>
					<li>Fabricates or alters a receipt, invoice, or payment confirmation.</li>
					<li>Fabricates or alters a bank balance, statement, or other financial record.</li>
					<li>Fabricates or alters a chat log, message thread, or other communication.</li>
					<li>Misrepresents the identity, statements, or actions of a real person or organization.</li>
					<li>Is otherwise intended to deceive a person, institution, or automated system relying on the image's authenticity.</li>
				</ul>
				<p>
					Legitimate use — localizing App Store screenshots, updating stale numbers in your own dashboard screenshots
					for a deck, fixing a typo in a screenshot you can no longer reproduce, redacting demo data, or swapping copy
					in your own UI mockups — is exactly what this tool is built for.
				</p>

				<h2>Content credentials</h2>
				<p>
					Every image exported from this service carries embedded content credentials (C2PA) marking it as edited. We
					do not offer a way to remove or hide this marking, at any pricing tier, for any reason.
				</p>

				<h2>Rate limits</h2>
				<p>
					Anonymous and free-tier use is rate-limited. We may throttle, suspend, or terminate access for any account or
					IP address we reasonably believe is violating these terms or attempting to circumvent rate limits.
				</p>

				<h2>Your content</h2>
				<p>
					You retain ownership of everything you upload. We process it only to provide the editing service — see our
					<a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a> for retention and deletion details.
				</p>

				<h2>No warranty</h2>
				<p>
					The service is provided as-is. We aim for pixel-accurate results and flag low-confidence matches instead of
					shipping a bad guess, but we don't guarantee a perfect result for every screenshot.
				</p>

				<h2>Contact</h2>
				<p>
					Questions about these terms can be sent to <a href="mailto:legal@screenshottexteditor.com">legal@screenshottexteditor.com</a>.
				</p>
			</Container>
		</section>
	</main>

	<Footer />
</Layout>

<style>
	.prose-content :global(h2) {
		margin-top: 2rem;
		font-size: 18px;
		font-weight: 600;
		letter-spacing: -0.01em;
		color: var(--color-ink);
	}
	.prose-content :global(p) {
		margin-top: 0.75rem;
	}
	.prose-content :global(ul) {
		margin-top: 0.75rem;
		list-style: disc;
		padding-left: 1.25rem;
	}
	.prose-content :global(li) {
		margin-top: 0.4rem;
	}
	.prose-content :global(a) {
		color: var(--color-link);
	}
	.prose-content :global(a:hover) {
		text-decoration: underline;
	}
</style>
